# WHAT THIS FILE DOES: stops the listed findings from failing `secret-scan`, so
# the gate can be added to a repo whose history already contains them.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO -- read this before trusting it:
#   - It rotates NOTHING. Nothing here has been rotated, revoked or re-issued.
#   - It removes nothing from git history. Every entry is still in the repo.
#   - It does not certify anything as fake. Entries are SHAPE-MATCHED by
#     gitleaks and assessed by path and context only. Liveness was NOT verified,
#     and could not be: confirming it means printing the value or presenting it
#     to an issuer.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:file:rule:line. No secret value is stored here, and
# each pins one exact known occurrence -- a NEW secret still fails the scan.
#
# WARNING: fingerprints are keyed to a COMMIT. Redacting or rewriting a flagged
# file creates a SECOND finding for the same content and re-breaks the gate. If
# you clean one of these up, expect to baseline the new fingerprint too.
